I was always involved as a DevOps & Infrastructure engineer in software projects, worked on many critical applications and delivering the necessary tools to confirm that the code is secure and ready in time, working perfectly in production.

I am not a developer, but I do have good knowledge of the Java development environment, worked on many applications in Python, ReactJS, and a little PHP — but again, not as a coder, but as a DevOps and infrastructure engineer, making sure everything else works and giving the developers the best environment possible to run their code.

I have implemented many complex database architectures such as Oracle RAC, DB2 pureScale, PGpool with PostgreSQL, AlwaysOn MS SQL, and others for mission-critical applications that require zero downtime. I have helped developers optimize their SQL queries, worked with data engineers on their ETL, tuned database engines, worked on backups and restores, and worked on best security practices for databases/apps.

I have had many projects where I had to migrate, by myself, legacy apps from old VMs (code in GitLab, barely any instructions on how to build or run it) to best practices and new technologies (building GitLab CI pipelines to build, test, check security, check code, and run on Kubernetes).

