What is your most senior role in a software engineering organisation? Describe your span of control, and the diversity of products, functions and teams you led.
I was the DevOps team lead in my previous experience. I was the guy who brought DevOps, DevSecOps and Kubernetes technologies for the first time to the bank — the person who got involved in all critical new applications and projects, bringing my expertise in designing and in the implementation.

My team was made of 6 amazing engineers with the label of the system infrastructure team, and I helped them get in touch with and learn all these new technologies at that time — from Docker/Kubernetes, to the DevOps toolchain (Ansible, GitLab CI, Jenkins, Nexus/Sonatype, SonarQube, OWASP ZAP and dependency check, ArgoCD, Harbor, Trivy…), to the observability stack with the ECK stack and LGTM stack.

We had the chance to migrate many critical apps, like the mobile bank app, from legacy Java on VMs with no DevOps philosophy, to the benefit of the DevOps CI/CD toolchain running on Kubernetes, and being well observed by LGTM — which improved the availability of the app to 99.9%, and gave us answers we could never give before, like: why is the app slow? Which version is where? Is it an infrastructure issue, a code issue, or a user issue?

Another chance we had was a major project bringing in a new Core Banking system, and even though it’s a very closed product, we managed to implement a CI/CD pipeline using Ansible and GitLab CI — improving time to market from weeks to minutes by automating every step possible across many teams.

